{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve had terrible diarrhea for two days—more than nine times a day. I also started vomiting, eight times yesterday, and the last one had a little blood in it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And any fever, chills, or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or chills. No black or bloody stools. But my stomach pain near the G-tube is worse, and I haven’t eaten since the diarrhea started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You were just discharged a week ago for similar pain, right? And you’re on oxycodone for that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. The pain is under control with the oxycodone, but only when I take it on schedule. Without it, it’s really bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ll make sure you get your pain meds on time. Now, you took loperamide—Imodium—for the diarrhea, and then the vomiting started?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my bariatric surgeon suggested it, but right after I took it, I felt nauseous and started vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s not uncommon. Sometimes slowing the gut down when there’s an infection can make nausea worse. We’ll hold off on Imodium for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. But why the blood in the vomit? I’m worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given that you vomited so many times, it’s likely from a small tear in the throat or stomach from the force—what we call a Mallory-Weiss tear. It’s usually minor and heals on its own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. That’s a relief. No more vomiting since I got here, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll give you IV fluids to rehydrate you and start a medication to help with nausea—ondansetron."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my G-tube? Should I be using it for feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-10-21 11:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. We’ll keep you on IV fluids and hold tube feeds until your diarrhea improves. We don’t want to stress your gut further."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-10-21 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back. Your electrolytes are a bit off—bicarb is low, which makes sense with all the vomiting—but nothing critical. Your kidney function and liver tests are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-10-21 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is my blood sugar okay? I usually check it because of my history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-10-21 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, glucose was 98, which is stable. No signs of hypoglycemia. We’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-10-21 15:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a simple X-ray—just to check your bowel gas pattern. No signs of obstruction or ileus. Everything looks okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-10-21 15:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. What about the stool test they took?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-10-21 15:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It came back positive for norovirus—specifically Norovirus GII. That explains the sudden vomiting and diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-10-21 15:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, like the stomach flu? Is it contagious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-10-21 15:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, very contagious. But we’re taking precautions. You’ll need to stay isolated for a few days, and your husband should wear gloves and wash hands well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-10-21 15:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure he knows. So it’s viral—no antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-10-21 15:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Antibiotics won’t help and could make it worse. We’re treating it supportively—fluids, rest, and letting it run its course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-10-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-10-22 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, I think. Only two episodes of diarrhea last night. Still nauseous, but not vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-10-22 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’ll start you on a light bariatric diet—small sips of clear liquids, then advance slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-10-22 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try a protein shake? I usually do well with those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-10-22 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let’s start with broth and apple juice. If you tolerate that, we can try a small amount of protein later. We don’t want to rush it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-10-22 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well this morning—no vomiting, and only one loose stool. Your electrolytes are improving too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-10-22 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I stop the IV now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-10-22 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it for now, but we’re close. We’ll switch to oral meds and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You had a good night—no diarrhea, no nausea. Labs this morning are normal. We think you’re ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s great! What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home with your usual meds—pantoprazole, sucralfate, oxycodone for pain, and ondansetron if nausea returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the dronabinol for appetite? I had a weird reaction last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll hold off on that for now. Your appetite should come back as you recover. We’ll discuss restarting it with your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my G-tube? I’ve been thinking—maybe it’s time to remove it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a conversation to have with your bariatric surgeon. Since you’re eating better, it might be possible. Follow up with them soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you, Doctor. I feel so much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-10-23 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Rest at home, stay hydrated, and call if symptoms return. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-10-21 11:05:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-10-23 17:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with severe diarrhea, nausea, and vomiting, following a recent hospitalization for chronic abdominal pain. She reported hematemesis after taking loperamide, which resolved with supportive care. Testing confirmed norovirus gastroenteritis, and she was managed with IV fluids, pain control, and gradual advancement to oral intake. Her symptoms improved, and she was discharged home on her prior medications, with plans to follow up with her bariatric surgeon regarding potential G-tube removal and her PCP for medication review.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute gastroenteropathy due to Norwalk agent",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Polyneuropathy, unspecified",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
